# Dependencies and build artifacts are (re)created inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
client/dist
**/dist

# The proprietary Pro workspace. This repository and every image built from it
# by default are AGPL-3.0; pro/ is not, and must never end up inside one.
#
# .gitignore already keeps it out of the repo, but Docker does not read
# .gitignore — without this line `COPY . .` in the builder stage pulls the
# proprietary source into an intermediate layer, which leaks the moment anyone
# builds with --target builder. The runtime stage's explicit COPY allowlist is
# what keeps it out of the published image today; this makes that a property of
# the build context rather than of nobody having edited those lines.
#
# The Pro image is built from pro/Dockerfile.pro, which BuildKit pairs with
# pro/Dockerfile.pro.dockerignore — a file that lives in the private repo and
# omits this entry on purpose. Both are absent from a public checkout, so the
# only build this repository can perform on its own is the AGPL one.
pro

# Local data + secrets never belong in the image.
data
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
.env
**/.env

# VCS, tooling, and docs that don't affect the build.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.claude
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
Caddyfile*
.dockerignore
*.md
